  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient is a 78\u2011year\u2011old woman with a long history of type 2 diabetes, hypertension, and coronary artery disease. Over the past decades she progressed from CKD stage 1 to stage 4 (onset 1998\u201112\u201111) and is currently awaiting kidney transplantation (since 1999\u201101\u201115). She suffered an acute ST\u2011segment elevation myocardial infarction in 1996 and has a history of coronary artery bypass grafting. She continues to experience angina requiring nitroglycerin spray and is on low\u2011dose amlodipine for blood pressure control. Diabetes\u2011related proteinuria and micro\u2011albuminuria have been documented since the early 1980s. Obesity (BMI\u202f\u2265\u202f30) and a remote history of breast cancer are also present. Socially, she reports chronic stress, isolation, limited contact, and a history of intimate\u2011partner abuse, which may affect adherence. The most recent encounter in the record is from December 2000, so current clinical status is uncertain and many recent labs are missing.",
